    5. For each distractor color, scatter 5-14 pixels randomly on remaining black cells, ensuring no color ever forms a solid 2x2 block. Allow occasional same-color adjacency.
    6. Verify the target rectangle is the unique largest solid >=2x2 rectangle across all colors (rejection check; virtually always passes since distractors have no 2x2 block).
